  },
  "articleBody": "When it comes to painting your bathroom, the sheen you choose isn't just about looks – it's about durability and how well it stands up to moisture. You'll often hear about semi-gloss and satin finishes for bathrooms, and for good reason. Both are more durable and easier to clean than flat or eggshell paints, which are better suited for less humid areas of your home. \n\n**Satin finish** has a soft, subtle sheen that's often described as velvety. It's a great choice for bathroom walls because it offers good moisture resistance and is quite washable without being overly shiny. It hides minor wall imperfections a bit better than a higher sheen would. \n\n**Semi-gloss finish**, on the other hand, has a more noticeable shine and is even more durable and easier to clean than satin. This makes it an excellent choice for trim, doors, and even cabinet exteriors in a bathroom, where they'll face more direct contact and splashes. Some people even prefer semi-gloss for walls in very high-traffic bathrooms for maximum protection. \n\nThe main trade-off is that higher sheens tend to highlight wall imperfections more. So, if your walls aren't perfectly smooth, satin might be a more forgiving choice. Ultimately, both are good options; it just depends on the level of shine and durability you're aiming for. Need help deciding or getting it done? HH Remodeling LLC is here to help.",
